outputs.What is 47 times 38?:
We can use the distributive property to break up the multiplication as follows:
\[
\begin{aligned}
47 \times 38 &= (40 + 7) \times 38 \\
&= 40 \times 38 + 7 \times 38 \\
&= 1520 + 266 \\
&= \boxed{1786}
\end{aligned}
\]
The answer is: 1786

